+# Agent Note: Opt-in vision sub-agent bridge for text-only models
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-22-text-model-vision-subagent-bridge.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Text-only main models cannot consume durable image blocks, but rejecting every image prevents them from using an independently deployed visual model. Sending historical image bytes to the main model is invalid for text-only providers, while automatically invoking a visual model for every upload spends latency and tokens when the request needs no pixel evidence. Historical lookup must also preserve session isolation and the append-only prefix used for KV-cache reuse.
+
+## Decision
+
+The base bundle contains `@deepseek-ai/dsh-vision-bridge` as an explicitly disabled plugin. A text-only deployment enables it through a composition overlay and configures one OpenAI-compatible visual model. Native multimodal deployments leave it disabled and keep the existing image route.
+
+When the agent loop claims a new human message containing images, the plugin appends one adjacent durable plugin notice after that message. The notice carries the complete attachment ids and says that the main model cannot read pixels directly. Existing events are never regenerated or reordered. The ordinary text-only request projection replaces image blocks with stable text handles, so the main model receives no data URL, base64 payload, or image token.
+
+The plugin registers `vision_inspect` only while it is loaded. The main model supplies current-conversation attachment ids and one self-contained visual task. The tool authorizes the complete id batch against the calling agent's full session event log before reading any bytes. It then sends the prompt and authorized images to the configured visual model and returns only `attachmentIds`, `summary`, `observations`, and `limitations`. Provider identity, endpoint, credential, timing, and untrusted extra response fields do not enter the tool result.
+
+Gateway routing and credentials remain deployment concerns. The endpoint comes from operator composition or the inherited process/user environment; a workspace `.env` cannot redirect it. The credential is resolved per call from the configured credential reference unless an explicitly embedded host credential is supplied. Transport failures use stable errors that do not include the endpoint, key, or remote response body.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Send every historical image to the main model.** Text-only providers cannot accept that request, and repeated image payloads consume context independently of textual history. Stable handles plus an explicit tool preserve a text-only main request.
+
+**Invoke the visual model immediately on every upload.** Some requests only store a reference, discuss filenames, or do not require pixel evidence. Model-directed inspection avoids mandatory visual latency and lets the prompt name the exact region, comparison, and evidence needed.
+
+**Execute XML-shaped tool calls found in private reasoning.** Text is not an authenticated structured tool call and may contain examples or malformed partial output. The bridge exposes only the native `vision_inspect` definition and never interprets reasoning text as an action.
+
+**Make the bridge a global preset capability.** Native multimodal routes already own image handling. Explicit composition enablement keeps the tool, reminder, and text-only admission behavior absent from deployments that do not need them.
+
+## Verification
+
+The package test owns every statement, branch, and function in the bridge implementation. It covers durable one-time reminders, text-only replay, current-session and cross-session authorization, request construction, literal/credential/environment key resolution, structured and malformed visual responses, limits, duplicate ids, cancellation, HTTP and JSON failures, redacted results, configuration rejection, contribution disposal, and reject/enter pre-step chaining. ACP content and API-proxy tests cover the shared image admission and model capability paths. A deployment test must also list the configured visual model through the gateway and complete one real image inspection before the overlay is promoted.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Each image-bearing human message adds one bounded durable text notice, and each inspection adds an ordinary tool call and text result. Historical notices remain reusable request-prefix text, but compaction summaries must retain complete attachment ids for the main model to select an obscured historical image. The bridge supports one configured visual backend and does not provide automatic failover or proactive inspection. Disabling or unloading it removes its admission provider, reminder hook, and tool registration without changing durable attachments or native multimodal behavior.
